.TH ANS2IRC 1 2026-10-16 "ans2irc 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ans2irc \- convert ANSI art to mIRC-coloured text for IRC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ans2irc
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ans2irc
reads ANSI art (CP437 text with escape codes, with or without a SAUCE record)
from
.I file
or standard input, and writes it as UTF-8 text with mIRC colour codes, one IRC
message per line, in as few bytes as the picture allows.
.PP
Each line is encoded in the fewest bytes that draw it: a space and a full
block in the same colour are interchangeable, as are a top half block and a
bottom half block with the colours reversed, and colour numbers take one digit
wherever the next character can't be read as part of them.
.PP
With a byte budget
.RB ( \-m
or
.BR \-f ),
a line that is still too long has its colours merged, a run of cells at a
time, until it fits; cells are cut from the right only when the glyphs alone
don't fit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " \fIN\fR"
Columns. The default is the SAUCE width, else 80.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-crop\-left " \fIN\fR"
Drop
.I N
columns from the left.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-crop\-right " \fIN\fR"
Drop
.I N
columns from the right.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tab\-size " \fIN\fR"
Tab stops every
.I N
columns. The default is 8.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-max\-bytes " \fIN\fR"
Fit every line in
.I N
bytes.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-for " \fIMASK TARGET\fR"
Fit every line in a message from
.I MASK
(nick!user@host) to
.I TARGET
(a channel or nick), as the people receiving it see it: 512 bytes less the
prefix the server adds.
.TP
.BR \-\-ice ", " \-\-no\-ice
Treat blink as a bright background, or as blink. The default is the SAUCE
flag, else
.BR \-\-ice .
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-swap\-shades
Let the encoder swap \[u2591] for \[u2593] with the colours reversed, and
\[u2592] either way round. The dither patterns differ slightly.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-colour
Plain text.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Report the number of lines, the longest line and any recolouring on standard
error.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the input can't be read, 2 for a bad option.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert a piece:
.PP
.RS
.B ans2irc art.ans > art.txt
.RE
.PP
Fit every line for messages from nick!user@host to #art:
.PP
.RS
.B ans2irc \-f 'nick!user@host' '#art' art.ans
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/mmoyles87/ans2irc
